From abc3b16214e9b974b36ad5584012be5502716dde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 04:49:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban-links): counts and task strip read one projection
 under links_reader=replica [daveey]

Under kanban.sync.links_reader=replica the sidebar counts read the origin-ledger
projection while session_tasks read the replica chat links, which dropped
done-but-unverified cards (Upkeep: "Waiting on 14 cards" over 9 chips).

- _remote_cards(None, ...) now feeds the counts too, so count and list come from
  one reader in each mode; the replica files are in the counts fingerprint.
- replica_cards: an unreleased link to a done/archived card, or to a card row the
  replica lacks, is an unknown, unfinished obligation; only a released link drops
  it. Only this origin profile's links (chat_profile) count. stale/synced_at come
  from the replica's real last pull (new kanban_sync_state.pulled_at, stamped by
  _pull_replica after a successful pull). An unreadable replica keeps its last
  rows (per path, gateway and profile) as stale; on a cold start it falls back to
  the ledger's rows for that board, stale. One row per (chat, card); the key
  carries the owner profile this chat's ledger row names, else default.
- annotate_kanban_activity counts a remote card shared by two sessions of one
  lineage once (it summed per-session rows; the list shows one row per card).
- links_diff compares unknown+unfinished obligations, never uses the ledger
  fallback, and is not clean while a replica it needs is unreadable, so it can no
  longer report clean while counts and list disagree.

Tests: test_kanban_chat_links_parity.py asserts count == listed rows for 1 active
+ 12 todo, review/blocked, done-unverified, missing card row (remote and own
gateway), old/never-pulled/fresh replica, unreadable replica warm, cold and per
profile, same id on two gateways, one owner profile per card, two origin profiles,
compression lineage (distinct and shared cards), verified release, another chat
turning done, and links_diff on unknown rows and unreadable replicas; the
pulled_at stamp test is in test_kanban_sync_client.py. The old replica test that
asserted a done unreleased card is NOT listed encoded the bug; it now asserts the
card is listed as unknown.
